  "about": "The epistola of the formulary “Nativity of the Lord — Mass during the Night” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "Dearly beloved: The grace of God our Savior has appeared to all men, teaching us that, denying ungodliness and worldly desires, we should live soberly, justly, and devoutly in this world, awaiting the blessed hope and the coming of the glory of the great God and our Savior Jesus Christ, who gave Himself for us, that He might redeem us from all iniquity and cleanse for Himself an acceptable people, a pursuer of good works. Speak these things and exhort, in Christ Jesus our Lord.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w005", "w006"], "anchor": "w005", "gloss": "our Savior" }, { "words": ["w035", "w036"], "anchor": "w035", "gloss": "our Savior" }, { "words": ["w053", "w054"], "anchor": "w053", "gloss": "an acceptable people" }, { "words": ["w065", "w066"], "anchor": "w065", "gloss": "our Lord" }] }
  },
